  "scope": "A second Pod uses the exact same executable and prompts with only the input guard disabled. Disposable Kubernetes v1.36.1 Pods run deterministic synthetic generation fixtures. The original in-process fixture has on/off branches for whitespace-token input and fake output, with fixed synthetic session IDs and a logical clock. The BPE HTTP fixture uses fixed template-expanded cl100k_base prompts, synthetic tokens, a guarded path and a same-worker input-guard-off comparison. The guarded serving container's effective CPU quota and memory cgroup ceiling are observed and compared with declared limits. This is container-bound evidence only; no CPU load, GPU, or cache validation. The HTTP fixture has no authenticated caller/session identity or concurrent generation. Neither fixture runs a real model or serving framework, configures a real KV cache, or measures GPU memory. Production route coverage, identity binding, concurrency, cache and device budgets, cgroup behavior, and monitoring require separate adopter evidence.",
